@@ precedence with the default list scope: an exception cancels deny rules
of its own list only; allow-mode lists win across lists.

-- list ads block adblock --
||example.org^
@@||safe.example.org^
||tracker.example^
@@|tracker.example^
-- list other block adblock --
||safe.example.org^
||shared.example^
-- list fix allow domains --
allowed.example.org
@@||alsoallowed.example^
-- counts ads --
rules=4 exceptions=2 unsupported=0 invalid=0 entries=4
-- counts fix --
rules=2 exceptions=0 entries=2
-- expect --
example.org               block ads ||example.org^
www.example.org           block ads ||example.org^
safe.example.org          block other ||safe.example.org^   # deviation: ads' @@ does not cancel other's deny
www.safe.example.org      block other ||safe.example.org^
tracker.example           allow ads @@|tracker.example^      # in-list exception, exact name only
www.tracker.example       block ads ||tracker.example^
allowed.example.org       allow fix allowed.example.org      # allow lists win across lists
www.allowed.example.org   block ads ||example.org^           # domain entries of allow lists are exact too
alsoallowed.example       allow fix ||alsoallowed.example^   # @@ in an allow list is an allow entry
x.alsoallowed.example     allow fix ||alsoallowed.example^
shared.example            block other ||shared.example^
unrelated.example         pass
